---
import LaunchLayout from "../layouts/LaunchLayout.astro";
import { PILOT_PRICE, REPOSITORY } from "../config/launch";
---
<LaunchLayout title="Paid pilot | Velvet" description="Scope a Velvet Outcome Assurance Pilot: one staging workflow, explicit business constraints, independent observations, and customer-owned regression checks.">
  <div class="l-wrap l-page">
    <div class="l-page-head"><p class="l-eyebrow">Outcome Assurance Pilot</p><h1>Start with the action<br />you need to trust.</h1><p class="l-lede">Before giving an agent more authority, establish what its controls actually prevent. Leave with a baseline and a project your own engineer can rerun.</p></div>
    <div class="l-split">
      <div class="l-prose"><h2>What we scope together</h2><p>One customer-owned staging workflow and two or three explicit business constraints. A refund limit, an account-state change, or approval expiry can be a useful starting point. The adapter and observation method must be feasible before work begins.</p><ol class="l-numbered"><li><strong>Define the outcome</strong><p>Agree the allowed and prohibited state, customer owner, declared routes, and acceptance criteria.</p></li><li><strong>Establish the baseline</strong><p>Run authorized isolated trials and independently observe the resulting business state. Label missing coverage and inconclusive observations.</p></li><li><strong>Remediate and retest</strong><p>Prioritize the observed gaps and perform one agreed remediation retest. Integration work outside the scope is quoted separately.</p></li><li><strong>Hand over the checks</strong><p>Your engineer reruns the customer-owned project and receives the report, limitations, and CI handoff instructions.</p></li></ol></div>
      <aside class="l-card"><span class="l-tag">Assisted · self-hosted</span><p class="l-price">{PILOT_PRICE}</p><p>Indicative starting price in Canadian dollars.</p><h3>Included in the starting scope</h3><ul><li>One workflow and an agreed route inventory</li><li>Baseline JSON and readable evidence report</li><li>Allowed-action controls as well as prohibited-action checks</li><li>Prioritized remediation plan and one retest</li><li>Customer-owned rerunnable project and handoff</li></ul><p class="l-fine">Planning target: 10 business days after scope, access, and prerequisites are agreed. Not a service-level commitment. Applicable taxes, the delivery schedule, and payment terms are confirmed in writing.</p><div class="l-actions"><a class="l-button" href="/contact/?intent=pilot">Request a scoping conversation ↗</a></div><a href={`${REPOSITORY}/blob/main/docs/public/customer-onboarding.md`}>Read the onboarding checklist</a></aside>
    </div>
    <div class="l-callout"><strong>A clean result is still a useful result.</strong><p>You are buying a bounded assessment and repeatable evidence, not a promise to find a vulnerability. A pilot does not establish that unknown or undeclared routes are safe.</p></div>
    <section class="l-page-section"><h2>Is this a fit?</h2><div class="l-grid"><article class="l-card"><h3>Bring an owner</h3><p>An engineer responsible for the business workflow and someone authorized to approve the testing scope. One person may cover both roles.</p></article><article class="l-card"><h3>Keep it isolated</h3><p>Use customer-controlled staging or a representative hermetic fixture, synthetic data, scoped test credentials, and a reset procedure. No production balances or customer records.</p></article><article class="l-card"><h3>Agree how to observe</h3><p>Provide read-only state observation where possible. A model's own explanation or an authorization log alone is not proof of the business outcome.</p></article></div></section>
    <section class="l-page-section l-prose"><h2>Before you commit</h2><details class="l-faq"><summary>Do we have to replace our gateway?</summary><p>No. Assessment can begin alongside your current controls. Inline Velvet enforcement is separate work and requires a supported boundary; it is not automatically included for every route.</p></details><details class="l-faq"><summary>Does the pilot need production credentials?</summary><p>No. The starting offer is limited to authorized isolated environments. Scope, credential handling, retention, and access removal are agreed before any access is provided.</p></details><details class="l-faq"><summary>What happens after the pilot?</summary><p>Decide whether to maintain these checks for future releases, add another workflow, or integrate supported enforcement. Ongoing coverage is separately scoped; there is no automatic subscription or renewal.</p></details><details class="l-faq"><summary>What is not included?</summary><p>Unrestricted third-party testing, a broad penetration test, guaranteed vulnerability discovery, production rollout, legal certification, insurance decisions, or round-the-clock incident response.</p></details></section>
    <div class="l-actions"><a class="l-button" href="/contact/?intent=pilot">Discuss your workflow ↗</a><a class="l-button l-button-quiet" href="/trust/">Review trust &amp; data handling</a></div>
  </div>
</LaunchLayout>
